@@ -3,3 +3,13 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, resolves a JSON
+Pointer string as defined in [RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901.html).
+For example, `resolvePointer({ items: ["first"] }, "/items/0")` returns `"first"`.
+An empty pointer returns the document itself; `~0` and `~1` in tokens refer to
+literal `~` and `/` characters. Invalid syntax and unresolved paths throw errors,
+including the nonexistent array element `-`. Pass a plain pointer string, rather
+than a URI fragment such as `#/items/0`. The document is not modified.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or later, with native TypeScript support).
